# Build context is the REPOSITORY ROOT (the Dockerfile COPYs engine/..., the
# workspace pyproject.toml and uv.lock, and LICENSE -- which lives at the root
# for AGPL compliance, see Dockerfile step 2a). Everything the image does not
# need is excluded here so the context stays small.

# Never ship a locally built environment or a tool cache. The image restores its
# own from uv.lock, and a host virtualenv carries absolute paths that are wrong
# inside a container.
.venv/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
engine/sandbox/
engine/data-raw/

# VCS / editor noise
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Untracked working files -- never part of an image.
CLAUDE.md
.private/
.token-optimizer/
.fastembed_cache/

# Layers that are not the engine. backend/pyproject.toml is the ONE exception
# and is re-admitted below: uv must be able to load every workspace member to
# honour the single root uv.lock, even though no backend code ships here.
backend/
!backend/pyproject.toml
!backend/README.md
!backend/src/**
frontend/
deploy/
docs/
# .github/ is excluded, with ONE exception re-admitted below: the manifest that
# run_verifications.sh reads its anti-vacuity floor from. Without it the floor
# silently degrades and the image's hard build gate stops asserting a minimum.
.github/
!.github/inventory.json

# docs that never enter the container
*.md.bak
